  "id": "DrugBank_DB01234 - MONDO_2289",
  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Iris Disease through a chain of indications that link it to Panuveitis, a condition that is further associated with Medrysone and Loteprednol Etabonate. These corticosteroids are commonly used in the treatment of inflammatory eye diseases, including Panuveitis, which is a key driver of Iris Disease. The evidence suggests that Dexamethasone may contribute to the development of Iris Disease through its anti-inflammatory effects, which are mediated by its ability to modulate immune responses and reduce inflammation in the eye. The overlapping indications across different corticosteroids highlight a potential mechanism by which these drugs could influence the progression of Iris Disease, possibly through shared pathways in inflammatory regulation. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of corticosteroids in the management of inflammatory conditions, suggesting a broader therapeutic relevance in the context of ocular inflammation.",
